ance) * step\x2C\x0d\n    dy: ((unit.y - nearest.y) / nearestDistance) * step\x2C\x0d\n    movementIntent: "minimum-range-retreat"\x2C\x0d\n  });\x0d\n}\x0d\n\x0d\n\x0d\n// Kited-world chase repath (measured\x2C kac archives): the recorded chasers do\x0d\n// not track their target's live position \u2014 their headings re-aim on a ~0.4-\x0d\n// 0.5 s cadence and their realized speed is p50 0.89 of the 1.056 dat speed\x0d\n// (path inefficiency)\x2C and their in-reach windows against a walking target\x0d\n// last only ~0.7-1.4 s where frictionless per-tick tracking holds reach\x0d\n// indefinitely (the sim glued tail produced 6-16 s windows the tape never\x0d\n// shows). Chasers therefore walk toward their pursuit target's position as\x0d\n// SAMPLED every repath interval\x2C per-unit phased; the stop rule still tests\x0d\n// the live target\x2C so a chaser that genuinely closes still halts and swings.\x0d\nconst KITE_CHASE_REPATH_TICKS = Math.round(0.5 * TICKS_PER_SECOND);\x0d\n\x0d\n\x0d\n// Genie movement is bimodal: a unit walks at its full dat speed or it stands\x0d\n// still. Across the kiting tapes the heavy camel's per-frame speed is 46.1% at\x0d\n// zero\x2C 52.9% between 1.50 and 1.70 against a dat 1.595\x2C and 0.6% anywhere in\x0d\n// between -- there is no population that grinds along a body. The constraint\x0d\n// solver manufactures one\x2C because it resolves a blocked step by removing only\x0d\n// its inward component and letting the remainder slide.\x0d\n//\x0d\n// A step the solver had to shorten is therefore taken as no step at all. It\x0d\n// cannot be cancelled after the fact -- the solve is simultaneous\x2C so a\x0d\n// neighbour may have moved into the space this unit was going to vacate -- so\x0d\n// the cancelled units are fed back in as stationary and the whole tick is\x0d\n// re-solved until the set stops growing. Each pass only ever adds to that set\x2C\x0d\n// so it terminates\x2C and the final pass is a normal solve with every invariant\x0d\n// intact. See docs/CAMEL_CHASER_GEOMETRY_2026-08-06.md.\x0d\nconst MAX_BIMODAL_PASSES = 8;\x0d\n// Floating-point tolerances only; no physical value is adjusted.\x0d\nconst STEP_EPSILON = 1e-9;\x0d\nconst ZERO_STEP_EPSILON = 1e-12;\x0d\n\x0d\n// A blocked unit does not stop dead in front of the body: it walks around it\x2C\x0d\n// at full speed. Cancelling without this strands the kite formation the moment\x0d\n// a chaser stands in its lane (duty cycle 0.18 against the tape's 0.79)\x2C and\x0d\n// the tape shows no such stranding.\x0d\n//\x0d\n// The search is a discretization\x2C not a physical constant: rotate the wanted\x0d\n// heading in fixed increments and take the smallest turn whose full-speed step\x0d\n// is clear\x2C preferring the left-hand turn on a tie so the result stays\x0d\n// deterministic. A unit that cannot clear its own body width within a quarter\x0d\n// turn is genuinely walled in and stands\x2C which is the tape's other mode.\x0d\nconst STEER_INCREMENT_RADIANS = Math.PI / 12;\x0d\nconst STEER_MAX_TURNS = 6;\x0d\n\x0d\n\x0d\nfunction stepClearsBodies(mover\x2C dx\x2C dy\x2C live\x2C bounds\x2C pairInteractions) {\x0d\n  const x = mover.x + dx;\x0d\n  const y = mover.y + dy;\x0d\n  const radius = collisionRadius(mover);\x0d\n  if (x < radius - STEP_EPSILON || x > bounds.width - radius + STEP_EPSILON\x0d\n    || y < radius - STEP_EPSILON || y > bounds.height - radius + STEP_EPSILON) return false;\x0d\n  for (const other of live) {\x0d\n    if (other.referenceId === mover.referenceId) continue;\x0d\n    const interaction = resolvePairInteraction(mover\x2C other\x2C pairInteractions);\x0d\n    if (!interaction.pathObstructs) continue;\x0d\n    const extent = interaction.collisionExtent;\x0d\n    if (Math.max(Math.abs(x - other.x)\x2C Math.abs(y - other.y)) < extent - STEP_EPSILON) {\x0d\n      return false;\x0d\n    }\x0d\n  }\x0d\n  return true;\x0d\n}\x0d\n\x0d\n\x0d\n// Does the wanted step hit at least one NON-TARGET enemy body? The chaser\x0d\n// steer fires only then:\x0d\n//   * ally blocks are a different regime -- KITER_FLOW measured real\x0d\n//     chaser-on-chaser stalls in the tape (kac champions 13.2% stall rate);\x0d\n//   * the mover's OWN pursuit/engagement target is the catch\x2C not an\x0d\n//     obstruction -- walking into it is how a chase ends\x2C and deflecting\x0d\n//     around it turns every would-be catch into an orbit (measured: with the\x0d\n//     target counted as a blocker\x2C every catching column flips -- kac 5v10\x2C\x0d\n//     esc 10v5\x2C hcp 20v15\x2C hcst 20v20 all lose their tape winner);\x0d\n//   * a NON-target enemy body is the ball surface\x2C which the camel forensics\x0d\n//     show the chaser routing around at full speed.\x0d\nfunction stepHitsAnyEnemyBody(mover\x2C dx\x2C dy\x2C live\x2C pairInteractions) {\x0d\n  const x = mover.x + dx;\x0d\n  const y = mover.y + dy;\x0d\n  for (const other of live) {\x0d\n    if (other.referenceId === mover.referenceId) continue;\x0d\n    if (other.owner === mover.owner) continue;\x0d\n    const interaction = resolvePairInteraction(mover\x2C other\x2C pairInteractions);\x0d\n    if (!interaction.pathObstructs) continue;\x0d\n    const extent = interaction.collisionExtent;\x0d\n    if (Math.max(Math.abs(x - other.x)\x2C Math.abs(y - other.y)) < extent - STEP_EPSILON) {\x0d\n      return true;\x0d\n    }\x0d\n  }\x0d\n  return false;\x0d\n}\x0d\n\x0d\n\x0d\nfunction stepHitsOtherEnemyBody(mover\x2C dx\x2C dy\x2C live\x2C pairInteractions) {\x0d\n  const x = mover.x + dx;\x0d\n  const y = mover.y + dy;\x0d\n  for (const other of live) {\x0d\n    if (other.referenceId === mover.referenceId) continue;\x0d\n    if (other.owner === mover.owner) continue;\x0d\n    if (other.referenceId === mover.pursuitTargetId\x0d\n      || other.referenceId === mover.engagedTargetId\x0d\n      || other.referenceId === mover.attackTargetId) continue;\x0d\n    const interaction = resolvePairInteraction(mover\x2C other\x2C pairInteractions);\x0d\n    if (!interaction.pathObstructs) continue;\x0d\n    const extent = interaction.collisionExtent;\x0d\n    if (Math.max(Math.abs(x - other.x)\x2C Math.abs(y - other.y)) < extent - STEP_EPSILON) {\x0d\n      return true;\x0d\n    }\x0d\n  }\x0d\n  return false;\x0d\n}\x0d\n\x0d\n\x0d\n\x0d\n\x0d\nfunction steerProposals(planned\x2C map\x2C chaserScopeOwner = null\x2C kitedEscape = false\x2C\n  movementOptions = {}) {\x0d\n  const pairInteractions = movementOptions.pairInteractions\x0d\n    ?? createPairInteractionSnapshot();\x0d\n  const hasMinimumRangeRetreat = planned.proposals.some(({ movementIntent }) => (\x0d\n    movementIntent === "minimum-range-retreat"\x0d\n  ));\x0d\n  if (!STEER_AROUND_BODIES && chaserScopeOwner === null && !hasMinimumRangeRetreat) {\x0d\n    return { proposals: planned.proposals\x2C steered: null };\x0d\n  }\x0d\n  const escapeActive = KITED_SIDE_STEER || kitedEscape;\x0d\n  const bounds = { width: map.width\x2C height: map.height };\x0d\n  const byReference = new Map(planned.units.map((unit) => [unit.referenceId\x2C unit]));\x0d\n  const steered = new Set();\x0d\n  const proposals = planned.proposals.map((proposal) => {\x0d\n    const distance = Math.hypot(proposal.dx\x2C proposal.dy);\x0d\n    if (distance <= ZERO_STEP_EPSILON) return proposal;\x0d\n    const mover = byReference.get(proposal.referenceId);\x0d\n    if (!mover) return proposal;\x0d\n    if (movementOptions.authoritativeReferenceIds?.has(mover.referenceId)) {\x0d\n      return proposal;\x0d\n    }\x0d\n    const minimumRangeRetreat = proposal.movementIntent === "minimum-range-retreat";\x0d\n    // "chaser" scope: only the chasing side of a kited scenario steers; the\x0d\n    // kiting side (and every non-kited fight) keeps the baseline solver.\x0d\n    // And only around NON-TARGET enemy bodies -- ally-blocked and\x0d\n    // target-blocked chasers keep the baseline solver (the tape's stall and\x0d\n    // catch regimes respectively).\x0d\n    if (!minimumRangeRetreat && !STEER_AROUND_BODIES) {\x0d\n      if (mover.owner === chaserScopeOwner) {\x0d\n        // "kited": the kiting side's MOVE-ORDERED units steer around enemy\x0d\n        // bodies too -- the tape's caught victim executes the scripted ball\x0d\n        // move through attacker contact at the ball's own pace\x2C where the\x0d\n        // baseline solver grinds it on the pressing chaser's body. Units\x0d\n        // without a move order (standing to shoot) keep the baseline. NO\x0d\n        // target exclusion here: a kiter's target is who it SHOOTS -- most\x0d\n        // often the very champion pressing it -- never a body it wants to\x0d\n        // walk into.\x0d\n        if (!escapeActive || !mover.moveOrder) return proposal;\x0d\n        if (!stepHitsAnyEnemyBody(\x0d\n          mover\x2C proposal.dx\x2C proposal.dy\x2C planned.units\x2C pairInteractions\x2C\x0d\n        )) {\x0d\n          return proposal;\x0d\n        }\x0d\n      } else {\x0d\n        // Steer only when the wanted step runs into a NON-TARGET enemy body\x0d\n        // (the ball surface). Ally blocks keep the baseline solver (the\x0d\n        // tape's chaser-on-chaser stalls are real)\x2C and the mover's own\x0d\n        // target is the catch. Wider triggers were measured and rejected --\x0d\n        // see the ally-queue ladder in HCC_CHASER_MOBILITY_2026-08-07.md.\x0d\n        if (!stepHitsOtherEnemyBody(\x0d\n          mover\x2C proposal.dx\x2C proposal.dy\x2C planned.units\x2C pairInteractions\x2C\x0d\n        )) {\x0d\n          return proposal;\x0d\n        }\x0d\n      }\x0d\n    }\x0d\n    if (stepClearsBodies(mover\x2C proposal.dx\x2C proposal.dy\x2C planned.units\x2C\x0d\n      bounds\x2C pairInteractions)) return proposal;\x0d\n    steered.add(proposal.referenceId);\x0d\n    const heading = Math.atan2(proposal.dy\x2C proposal.dx);\x0d\n    // Retreaters keep a stable parity-selected side on symmetric choices.\x0d\n    // This is deterministic per unit and avoids steering an entire siege\x0d\n    // cohort into the same new queue. Recomputing around the current threat\x0d\n    // heading each tick lets the route follow a moving pinner without a\x0d\n    // calibrated turn timer.\x0d\n    const sides = minimumRangeRetreat && mover.referenceId % 2 !== 0\x0d\n      ? [-1\x2C 1]\x0d\n      : [1\x2C -1];\x0d\n    for (let turn = 1; turn <= STEER_MAX_TURNS; turn += 1) {\x0d\n      for (const side of sides) {\x0d\n        const angle = heading + side * turn * STEER_INCREMENT_RADIANS;\x0d\n        const dx = Math.cos(angle) * distance;\x0d\n        const dy = Math.sin(angle) * distance;\x0d\n        if (stepClearsBodies(mover\x2C dx\x2C dy\x2C planned.units\x2C bounds\x2C\x0d\n          pairInteractions)) {\x0d\n          return Object.freeze({ ...proposal\x2C dx\x2C dy });\x0d\n        }\x0d\n      }\x0d\n    }\x0d\n    return Object.freeze({ ...proposal\x2C dx: 0\x2C dy: 0 });\x0d\n  });\x0d\n  return { proposals\x2C steered };\x0d\n}\n\n\nfunction fourWayPursuitCliques(units\x2C pursuitReferenceIds\x2C padding = 0) {\n  const byOwner = new Map();\n  for (const unit of units) {\n    if (!pursuitReferenceIds.has(unit.referenceId) || unit.alive === false) continue;\n    if (!byOwner.has(unit.owner)) byOwner.set(unit.owner\x2C []);\n    byOwner.get(unit.owner).push(unit);\n  }\n  const overlaps = (left\x2C right) => Math.max(\n    Math.abs(left.x - right.x)\x2C\n    Math.abs(left.y - right.y)\x2C\n  ) < collisionRadius(left) * left.mechanics.min_collision_size_multiplier\n    + collisionRadius(right) * right.mechanics.min_collision_size_multiplier\n    + padding - STEP_EPSILON;\n  const result = [];\n  for (const allies of byOwner.values()) {\n    allies.sort((left\x2C right) => left.referenceId - right.referenceId);\n    for (let a = 0; a < allies.length; a += 1) {\n      for (let b = a + 1; b < allies.length; b += 1) {\n        if (!overlaps(allies[a]\x2C allies[b])) continue;\n        for (let c = b + 1; c < allies.length; c += 1) {\n          if (!overlaps(allies[a]\x2C allies[c]) || !overlaps(allies[b]\x2C allies[c])) continue;\n          for (let d = c + 1; d < allies.length; d += 1) {\n            if ([a\x2C b\x2C c].every((index) => overlaps(allies[index]\x2C allies[d]))) {\n              result.push([allies[a]\x2C allies[b]\x2C allies[c]\x2C allies[d]]\n                .map(({ referenceId }) => referenceId));\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return result;\n}\n\n\nfunction fourWayPursuitRisk(units\x2C pursuitReferenceIds\x2C padding) {\n  const cliques = fourWayPursuitCliques(units\x2C pursuitReferenceIds\x2C padding);\n  const byReference = new Map(units.map((unit) => [unit.referenceId\x2C unit]));\n  let depth = 0;\n  for (const clique of cliques) {\n    let shallowestPairDepth = Infinity;\n    for (let leftIndex = 0; leftIndex < clique.length; leftIndex += 1) {\n      const left = byReference.get(clique[leftIndex]);\n      for (let rightIndex = leftIndex + 1; rightIndex < clique.length; rightIndex += 1) {\n        const right = byReference.get(clique[rightIndex]);\n        const separation = Math.max(\n          Math.abs(left.x - right.x)\x2C\n          Math.abs(left.y - right.y)\x2C\n        );\n        const surface = collisionRadius(left)\n            * left.mechanics.min_collision_size_multiplier\n          + collisionRadius(right)\n            * right.mechanics.min_collision_size_multiplier\n          + padding;\n        shallowestPairDepth = Math.min(shallowestPairDepth\x2C surface - separation);\n      }\n    }\n    depth += Math.max(0\x2C shallowestPairDepth);\n  }\n  return {\n    // A simultaneous pair can legitimately cross by the sum of both sourced\n    // one-tick movement budgets. Count a four-body pile only once it is deeper\n    // than that kinematic transit band; the positively padded graph below\n    // still prevents a shallow crossing from becoming a sustained collapse.\n    actualCount: fourWayPursuitCliques(\n      units\x2C pursuitReferenceIds\x2C -padding\x2C\n    ).length\x2C\n    cliques\x2C\n    depth\x2C\n  };\n}\n\n\nfunction crowdRiskImproves(candidate\x2C current) {\n  if (candidate.actualCount !== current.actualCount) {\n    return candidate.actualCount < current.actualCount;\n  }\n  if (candidate.cliques.length !== current.cliques.length) {\n    return candidate.cliques.length < current.cliques.length;\n  }\n  return candidate.depth < current.depth - STEP_EPSILON;\n}\n\n\nfunction rotateMovementProposal(proposal\x2C side\x2C turn) {\n  const distance = Math.hypot(proposal.dx\x2C proposal.dy);\n  const angle = Math.atan2(proposal.dy\x2C proposal.dx)\n    + side * turn * Math.PI / 12;\n  return Object.freeze({\n    ...proposal\x2C\n    dx: Math.cos(angle) * distance\x2C\n    dy: Math.sin(angle) * distance\x2C\n  });\n}\n\n\nfunction repairFourWayPursuitCrowding(\n  snapshot\x2C proposals\x2C moved\x2C map\x2C movementOptions\x2C preparedMovement\x2C\n) {\n  const pursuitReferenceIds = movementOptions.pairInteractions\n    ?.pursuitTransitReferenceIds ?? new Set();\n  if (pursuitReferenceIds.size === 0) return moved;\n  const beforeByReference = new Map(snapshot.map((unit) => [unit.referenceId\x2C unit]));\n  const baseByReference = new Map(proposals.map((row) => [row.referenceId\x2C row]));\n  const chosen = [...proposals].sort((left\x2C right) => (\n    left.referenceId - right.referenceId\n  ));\n  const chosenIndexByReference = new Map(chosen.map((proposal\x2C index) => (\n    [proposal.referenceId\x2C index]\n  )));\n  let result = moved;\n  const pursuitStepLengths = proposals\n    .filter(({ referenceId }) => pursuitReferenceIds.has(referenceId))\n    .map(({ dx\x2C dy }) => Math.hypot(dx\x2C dy))\n    .sort((left\x2C right) => right - left);\n  // Maximum one-tick pair closure comes from both bodies moving\x2C so the\n  // no-four-stack guard looks ahead by the sum of the two largest sourced\n  // movement budgets rather than by an arbitrary safety margin.\n  const lookaheadPadding = (pursuitStepLengths[0] ?? 0)\n    + (pursuitStepLengths[1] ?? 0);\n  const trialOptions = () => (movementOptions.collisionRecoveryState\n    ? { ...movementOptions\x2C collisionRecoveryState: {\n      active: movementOptions.collisionRecoveryState.active === true\x2C\n    } }\n    : movementOptions);\n\n  for (let pass = 0; pass < pursuitReferenceIds.size * 2; pass += 1) {\n    const currentRisk = fourWayPursuitRisk(\n      result\x2C pursuitReferenceIds\x2C lookaheadPadding\x2C\n    );\n    if (currentRisk.cliques.length === 0) return result;\n    const involved = new Set(currentRisk.cliques.flat());\n    const actualCliquesNow = fourWayPursuitCliques(\n      result\x2C pursuitReferenceIds\x2C -lookaheadPadding\x2C\n    );\n    const actualInvolvedNow = new Set(actualCliquesNow.flat());\n    const candidates = [...involved]\n      .map((referenceId) => {\n        const unit = beforeByReference.get(referenceId);\n        const target = beforeByReference.get(unit?.pursuitTargetId);\n        const proposal = baseByReference.get(referenceId);\n        return { unit\x2C target\x2C proposal };\n      })\n      .filter(({ unit\x2C target\x2C proposal }) => (\n        unit && target?.alive && target.owner !== unit.owner\n        && proposal && Math.hypot(proposal.dx\x2C proposal.dy) > STEP_EPSILON\n      ))\n      .sort((left\x2C right) => {\n        const leftDistance = Math.hypot(\n          left.target.x - left.unit.x\x2C left.target.y - left.unit.y\x2C\n        );\n        const rightDistance = Math.hypot(\n          right.target.x - right.unit.x\x2C right.target.y - right.unit.y\x2C\n        );\n        return rightDistance - leftDistance\n          || left.unit.referenceId - right.unit.referenceId;\n      });\n    const variantsFor = ({ unit\x2C proposal }\x2C { forwardOnly = true } = {}) => {\n      const variants = [];\n      const preferredSide = unit.referenceId % 2 === 0 ? 1 : -1;\n      for (let turn = 1; turn < (forwardOnly ? 6 : 12); turn += 1) {\n        for (const side of [preferredSide\x2C -preferredSide]) {\n          const candidate = rotateMovementProposal(proposal\x2C side\x2C turn);\n          if (forwardOnly\n              && candidate.dx * proposal.dx + candidate.dy * proposal.dy <= STEP_EPSILON) {\n            continue;\n          }\n          variants.push({ unit\x2C proposal\x2C candidate\x2C side\x2C turn });\n        }\n      }\n      return variants;\n    };\n    const evaluate = (changes\x2C { requireForward = true } = {}) => {\n      const trialProposals = chosen.slice();\n      for (const { unit\x2C candidate } of changes) {\n        trialProposals[chosenIndexByReference.get(unit.referenceId)] = candidate;\n      }\n      let trial;\n      try {\n        trial = resolvePreparedMovementProposals(\n          preparedMovement\x2C\n          trialProposals\x2C\n          trialOptions()\x2C\n        );\n      } catch {\n        return null;\n      }\n      const risk = fourWayPursuitRisk(\n        trial\x2C pursuitReferenceIds\x2C lookaheadPadding\x2C\n      );\n      if (!crowdRiskImproves(risk\x2C currentRisk)) return null;\n      const trialByUnit = new Map(trial.map((unit) => [unit.referenceId\x2C unit]));\n      for (const { unit\x2C proposal } of changes) {\n        const after = trialByUnit.get(unit.referenceId);\n        const actualDx = after.x - unit.x;\n        const actualDy = after.y - unit.y;\n        const wantedDistance = Math.hypot(proposal.dx\x2C proposal.dy);\n        if (Math.hypot(actualDx\x2C actualDy) < wantedDistance - STEP_EPSILON) return null;\n        if (requireForward\n            && actualDx * proposal.dx + actualDy * proposal.dy <= STEP_EPSILON) return null;\n      }\n      return { changes\x2C risk\x2C trial };\n    };\n    let best = null;\n    let firstImprovement = null;\n    const primaryCandidates = currentRisk.actualCount > 0\n      ? candidates.filter(({ unit }) => actualInvolvedNow.has(unit.referenceId))\n      : candidates;\n    candidateSearch:\n    for (const row of primaryCandidates) {\n      for (const variant of variantsFor(row)) {\n          const ranked = evaluate([variant]);\n          if (ranked === null) continue;\n          if (currentRisk.actualCount > 0\n              && ranked.risk.actualCount >= currentRisk.actualCount) {\n            if (firstImprovement === null) firstImprovement = ranked;\n            continue;\n          }\n          // Candidate enumeration is already the physical priority order:\n          // rearmost chaser\x2C smallest positive turn\x2C stable preferred side.\n          // The first improving result is therefore the shortest admissible\n          // correction; evaluating every wider turn only repeats expensive\n          // collision solves without changing that decision.\n          best = ranked;\n          break candidateSearch;\n      }\n    }\n    if (best === null && currentRisk.actualCount === 0) best = firstImprovement;\n    if (best === null && currentRisk.actualCount > 0) {\n      // A perfectly symmetric four-body knot can require two allies to peel in\n      // opposite directions before either individual turn improves the graph.\n      // Search that pair only after every one-body correction failed. Each\n      // member still moves at full sourced speed with a positive component on\n      // its pursuit heading; this is decongestion\x2C never a reverse order.\n      const actualInvolved = new Set(fourWayPursuitCliques(\n        result\x2C pursuitReferenceIds\x2C -lookaheadPadding\x2C\n      ).flat());\n      const pairVariants = candidates\n        .filter(({ unit }) => actualInvolved.has(unit.referenceId))\n        .flatMap(variantsFor);\n      pairSearch:\n      for (let left = 0; left < pairVariants.length; left += 1) {\n        for (let right = left + 1; right < pairVariants.length; right += 1) {\n          if (pairVariants[left].unit.referenceId\n              === pairVariants[right].unit.referenceId) continue;\n          best = evaluate([pairVariants[left]\x2C pairVariants[right]]);\n          if (best !== null) break pairSearch;\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    if (best === null && currentRisk.actualCount > 0) {\n      // If an enemy body or static corner makes every targetward separation\n      // impossible\x2C remaining inside a four-body allied knot is worse than a\n      // one-tick outward peel. Take the smallest full-speed physical escape;\n      // the ordinary pursuit proposal is recomputed on the next tick.\n      const actualCliques = fourWayPursuitCliques(\n        result\x2C pursuitReferenceIds\x2C -lookaheadPadding\x2C\n      );\n      // Resolve one concrete knot atomically. Using the union of every knot\n      // makes a candidate that fixes one look neutral when another remains\x2C\n      // and lets unrelated corrections consume the pass budget.\n      const actualInvolved = new Set(actualCliques[0]);\n      const resultByReference = new Map(result.map((unit) => [unit.referenceId\x2C unit]));\n      const crowdedRows = [...actualInvolved]\n        .map((referenceId) => {\n          const unit = beforeByReference.get(referenceId);\n          return {\n            unit\x2C\n            target: beforeByReference.get(unit?.pursuitTargetId)\x2C\n            proposal: baseByReference.get(referenceId)\x2C\n          };\n        })\n        .filter(({ unit\x2C target\x2C proposal }) => (\n          unit && target?.alive && target.owner !== unit.owner && proposal\n        ));\n      const awayVariants = crowdedRows.map(({ unit\x2C proposal }) => {\n          const clique = actualCliques.find((ids) => ids.includes(unit.referenceId));\n          const peers = clique\n            .filter((referenceId) => referenceId !== unit.referenceId)\n            .map((referenceId) => resultByReference.get(referenceId));\n          const current = resultByReference.get(unit.referenceId);\n          const centerX = peers.reduce((sum\x2C peer) => sum + peer.x\x2C 0) / peers.length;\n          const centerY = peers.reduce((sum\x2C peer) => sum + peer.y\x2C 0) / peers.length;\n          let awayX = current.x - centerX;\n          let awayY = current.y - centerY;\n          let length = Math.hypot(awayX\x2C awayY);\n          if (length <= STEP_EPSILON) {\n            awayX = unit.referenceId % 2 === 0 ? -proposal.dy : proposal.dy;\n            awayY = unit.referenceId % 2 === 0 ? proposal.dx : -proposal.dx;\n            length = Math.hypot(awayX\x2C awayY);\n          }\n          const distance = Math.max(\n            Math.hypot(proposal.dx\x2C proposal.dy)\x2C\n            unit.mechanics.speed_tiles_per_second / TICKS_PER_SECOND\x2C\n          );\n          return {\n            unit\x2C\n            proposal\x2C\n            candidate: Object.freeze({\n              ...proposal\x2C\n              dx: awayX / length * distance\x2C\n              dy: awayY / length * distance\x2C\n            })\x2C\n            side: 0\x2C\n            turn: 0\x2C\n          };\n        });\n      const enemySurfaceTangents = crowdedRows.flatMap(({ unit\x2C target\x2C proposal }) => {\n        const distance = Math.max(\n          Math.hypot(proposal.dx\x2C proposal.dy)\x2C\n          unit.mechanics.speed_tiles_per_second / TICKS_PER_SECOND\x2C\n        );\n        const targetDx = target.x - unit.x;\n        const targetDy = target.y - unit.y;\n        const alongXFace = Math.abs(targetDx) >= Math.abs(targetDy);\n        return [-1\x2C 1].map((side) => ({\n          unit\x2C\n          proposal\x2C\n          candidate: Object.freeze({\n            ...proposal\x2C\n            dx: alongXFace ? 0 : side * distance\x2C\n            dy: alongXFace ? side * distance : 0\x2C\n          })\x2C\n          side\x2C\n          turn: 0\x2C\n        }));\n      });\n      const exactEscapeVariants = [...awayVariants\x2C ...enemySurfaceTangents];\n      for (const variant of exactEscapeVariants) {\n        best = evaluate([variant]\x2C { requireForward: false });\n        if (best !== null) break;\n      }\n      if (best === null